+# Captain Notes
+
+## Browser-only defect: Edit handler double-fire
+
+The acceptance suite (Cypress, real browser) reports `NotFoundError: Failed to execute 'removeChild' on 'Node'` when editing a todo with empty text and pressing Enter.
+
+**Root cause:** Both the `keydown` handler (Enter) and the `blur` handler (capture phase) call `editTodo` and `render`. In a real browser, removing a focused `<li>` via `removeChild` fires `blur` synchronously. The blur handler re-processes the same edit, triggering a nested `render()` inside the outer `render()`'s removal loop, which fails because the node was already detached.
+
+**Why the harness passes:** happy-dom does not fire `blur` synchronously on `removeChild`. The in-harness suite never exercises the nested-render path.
+
+**Spec status:** The existing product spec `features/todos.feature:Editing with empty input removes the todo` is correct and unchanged. The defect is in the implementation, not the spec.
+
+**Conformance guard:** `features/edit-conformance.feature` adds a `@conformance` scenario that checks the source code for a guard in the blur handler. This scenario WILL fail on the current code because no guard exists. It is listed in `watchbill.json` as the sole watch target for the next QM dispatch.
+
+**Next steps:** QM implements the step definitions for the conformance scenario. Crew adds a guard (e.g., a flag or conditional) so the blur handler defers when Enter has already processed the edit. The existing product spec should then pass in a real browser.
